---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About" description="About nth degree">
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>About</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="content">
    <p>
      nth degree is a personal blog about infrastructure, networking, and homelab engineering.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every setup here runs in a Proxmox cluster in my garage. The writing covers what
      I've built, broken, and fixed: bare-metal networking, container orchestration,
      monitoring stacks, storage.
    </p>

    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Static site</strong> using Astro / TypeScript, deployed on Cloudflare Workers</li>
      <li><strong>Source</strong> on GitHub with pre-commit checks for quality</li>
      <li><strong>No CSS frameworks or client JavaScript</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Writing</h2>
    <p>
      One idea per post. No fluff. Specifics over generalities:
      <q>Caddy with a Let's Encrypt TLS cert</q> not <q>good security.</q>
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Typeset in <a href="https://rsms.me/inter/">Inter</a> with
      <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/">JetBrains Mono</a> for code.
      Colors adapt to your system light/dark preference.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
